  "title": "Nerka E NDE 6625",
  "date": "08/18/1989",
  "content": "My daughter was born by natural childbirth in the hospital operating room. About fifteen to thirty minutes after the delivery, I told the nurse that I wasn't feeling well. I felt like I was going to pass out. That is all that I can remember of being my normal self before things started happening. I never lost my hearing. I could hear every word the nurses said. I heard them say that my blood pressure was going down to eighty over sixty, and that they were not able to start an IV because my veins were collapsed. I heard the doctors screaming about losing a patient. In my mind, I was going down a dark tunnel. I saw many pictures of myself from my childhood to that present moment in the operating room. Then I was ‘above’ my body, looking down on myself. I also saw several nurses and two doctors from above. After that, I was ‘back.’",
